  "mechanismSummary": "Ethoxide forms the enolate of the side-chain methyl ketone. It attacks the ring ketone, closing a new six-membered ring, and ethanol protonates the alkoxide. A second enolate forms next to the carbon carrying OH and pushes out hydroxide (E1cB), giving the conjugated bicyclic enone. With the Michael addition before it, this is the Robinson annulation: a new six-membered ring with an enone in it.",
